From e9c1fdfda922c91c05464156d1577e07945d82e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:43:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-x1e80100: keep the display AXI clock until the
 display driver takes it

The firmware leaves the display engine scanning out its boot framebuffer (the vendor logo) when it starts the
kernel. The unused-clock pass at late_initcall_sync switches gcc_disp_hf_axi_clk off long before the display clock
controller and the display driver, both modules, have probed, i.e. in the middle of a scanout.

On the ASUS Vivobook S 15 (X1E80100) everything after that point ran several times slower until the display driver
reset the display engine about 20 s into the boot: unpacking the rest of the initramfs, the module loads, the NVMe
bring-up, the TPM unlock, userspace. Measured with the same kernel: initramfs 7.6-9.4 s instead of 2.0 s, userspace
(to the display manager) 13.0 s instead of 3.5 s, whole boot 29-31 s instead of 13.7 s. clk_ignore_unused had the
same effect, pd_ignore_unused had none, and holding only this clock (a simple-framebuffer node with it as its clock)
was enough. The most likely mechanism: the display engine is a real-time client of the memory controller, and with
its memory path cut it keeps signalling underflow ("danger"), which throttles every other client. The screen also
went black at that moment.

Mark the clock CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED. The display driver takes it over at probe and switches it off in runtime suspend,
so idle and standby are unchanged once the driver is loaded.

Not upstream.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c
index 8c146d62c..2ba4b1ecf 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-x1e80100.c
@@ -2998,6 +2998,11 @@ static struct clk_branch gcc_disp_hf_axi_clk = {
 		.enable_mask = BIT(0),
 		.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
 			.name = "gcc_disp_hf_axi_clk",
+			/*
+			 * The firmware leaves the display engine scanning out its boot framebuffer.
+			 * Keep its memory path until the display driver (a module) takes the clock.
+			 */
+			.flags = CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED,
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
 		},
 	},
-- 
2.43.0

